# Cloudflare Pages SPA routing.
#
# React Router owns every path below /, but Cloudflare serves static files: a
# hard load or refresh of /insights asks for a file that was never built and
# gets a 404. This rewrites unmatched paths to the app shell so the router can
# resolve them client-side.
#
# Status 200 makes it a rewrite, not a redirect - the browser keeps the
# original URL. This is the Cloudflare equivalent of the `rewrites` block in
# frontend/vercel.json; both files are kept so either host can serve the app.
#
# Vite copies public/ to the root of dist/, which is what `wrangler pages
# deploy dist` uploads, so this needs no build-config change.
/*    /index.html   200
